WEBVTT

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.440
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.780
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.410
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.910
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.460
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.090
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.680
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.390
by ridding you...

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.560
...of your other love?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.150
At sunset,

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.650
when the children go home,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.570
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:58.490
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.580
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.370
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.000
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.880
In a city without light,

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.720
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.140
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.430
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.930
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.610
I'm Kurata Sana,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.110
a 6th grader and TV personality
affiliated with Gekidan Komawari.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.120
My beloved Mama is a famous novelist,
who has even won the Aoki Laureate Prize.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.120
And that's her chipmunk,
Maro-chan.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.870
My former boyfriend,
Sagami Rei-kun.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.460
Right now, he's earnestly on the way
to becoming a fine manager.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.130
The mysterious white bat
straight man, Babbit.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.630
My liquid diet is delicious.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.630
Hayama Akito,
my natural enemy.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:59.140
Even so, right now, when I'm around him,
I'm relaxed for some reason.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.140
Hayama...

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.140
What are you doing?

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.140
What is that thing!?

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:10.810
Well, you know... I'm not sure
what it is, but it's yours.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.820
After the middle birthday party
and Christmas Eve party ended,

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.820
--just as I was breathing easy...
--A present?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.820
...suddenly,
I was kissed by Hayama!

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.830
I got kissed!
I got kissed! I got kissed!

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.170
But this time,
I couldn't avoid him, you know?

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.420
Could this be...
could this be my first kiss?

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.430
But before I had a chance to think,
the Kurata household was in big trouble!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.100
The Kurata household...
has gone bankrupt.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:50.100
B- b- bankrupt!?

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.610
"Suddenly, One Day,
I'm a Homeless Girl"

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:57.110
Oh, my. There's red paper
hanging off of everything.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.450
Whoa, everything in here, too!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.780
Oh, dear, in here, too.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.790
Seized... seized...

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:09.460
Oh, Sana-chan's room
has seizure papers on everything-

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:14.130
"Seized"

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:12.460
Uh... um, what happens to everything
that has been seized?

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.130
You can't use it.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.460
Then, Babbit can't be used,
either? Farewell!

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.130
That's just a supermarket receipt,
so it doesn't have any bearing.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.090
What!? Thank goodness!
But don't be so misleading!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.810
What exactly is going on?

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.140
There's nothing more to it.
Bankrupt means bankrupt.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.440
But that means that all of your
property will be seized, right?

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.730
Which explains why the gentlemen
from the tax office

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.400
are all working so hard
right now, doesn't it?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.900
"Doesn't it?"

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.950
How can you say it so casually!?
What on earth happened!?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.450
Well, you see...

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.290
Click...

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:51.080
♪ There was once a certain company, ♪

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.630
♪ that was trying to get
a loan from the bank. ♪

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:58.420
♪ I was the guarantor on the loan, ♪

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.090
♪ a guarantor that I should not have been. ♪

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.760
♪ Then the company went under, hey! ♪

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:09.430
♪ and the debt came crashing
down on my shoulders. ♪

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:13.100
♪ In other words, I, too
am bankrupt, bankrupt. ♪

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.810
♪ Since I am the guarantor,
there's nothing I can do. ♪

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.150
This is no time to be
explaining things in song.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.490
Why not?

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.490
Ah! Even my Nopia!

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:27.160
Sensei, this... this is a serious matter!
This is a serious matter, Sensei!

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.450
I know.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.750
Why did you trust
those people so easily?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.080
It's not about whether
I trusted them or not.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.420
It's fate.
This is all fate.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.090
Fate? Is that the reason why you didn't care
if all of your property was taken from you?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.420
It could be.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.430
What are you planning to do now?

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.100
Now, now, Rei-kun, calm down.
Ultimately, this is all a nightmare.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:53.770
Once we wake up, we'll say
"Ah, it was just a dream!"

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.100
Even so,

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.940
with a man here whose face is as
expressionless as his, this is not reality.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.530
Huh? I am Okouchi,
from the tax office.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.360
You'll have to excuse
my expressionless face,

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.200
but this is real.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:10.030
Whoa, for having an expressionless face,
that was quite a dramatic touch.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.040
Well then,
might I have a moment?

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.040
What do you want?

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.370
Tell me, if you were to take a lady out
on a date, what course would you select?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.500
Let's see...
Of course,

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:22.380
I would wait for her in front of the statue
of Saigo Takamori, in Ueno Park.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.050
We would visit the art gallery
and the museum,

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.390
and then we would go
to a classical music coffeehouse,

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.720
and talk about our futures
over slightly bitter espressos.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.890
That is the way
a date should be.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.730
You have a severe personality, where
everything is measured with a square rule.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:37.730
Oh, dear...

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.900
This, despite having
such a round face.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:44.900
If I may, as of right now,
this house is the property of the state.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.070
You are being
evicted immediately!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.950
Evicted?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.550
What's... going on?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:14.560
It was all so sudden...
it just happened all at once...

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.560
How can we be...
standing here...

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:23.400
gazing at the house...
we've been living in for so long?

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.910
Come on,
let's get going.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.760
Don't cry,
Shimura-san.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:51.930
Sensei, Sana-chan... Sagami-san,
you all take good care of yourselves, now.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.760
You too.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.100
Shimura-san, we're really
grateful for everything.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.100
Shimura-san...

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.020
We'll be able to see each other
again soon, right?

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.360
--Of course we will.
--Shimura-san...

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.860
Sana-chan!

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.530
Shimura-san!
I'll never forget...

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.040
I'll never forget the taste
of your Thai-style curry!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.050
Shimura-san...

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:40.060
What about asking the folks back home
in Kusatsu if they could help out somehow?

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.060
For what reason?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.900
For what reason? So that we can
go on living the way we always have.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.400
In life, there are mountains,
and there are valleys.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.400
We're raking it in
just by being alive.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.410
That's right! It's not as though
they've taken our lives from us, huh?

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.070
We won't get anywhere
if we just flap around, will we?

00:07:55.070 --> 00:08:00.080
Oh, that's my girl. The rain
should stop sometime tomorrow, too.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.710
Sensei! Sensei!
I found something!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.010
"This is their new home?"

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:09.170
A cooperative apartment!

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.840
This is the apartment
that I lived in before.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.390
It has been vacant ever since.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:17.050
The media won't
find you here, either.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:24.020
Uh, it's not to your liking, then?
I'd suppose not. It's dirty and cramped.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.070
It has walls.
It has windows.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:29.690
And more than that,
it has a roof.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.360
Mama, it also has
a pillar for no reason.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.030
Thank you, Onda.
We're grateful.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.740
Not at all.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.080
Sana! We'll climb our way out of here
to reach for tomorrow's stars!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.370
Mm-hmm, that we will, Mama!

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.750
Look! That will be the star
you reach for, Sana!

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:43.750
Which one?
Mama, which one?

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.040
It's raining tonight.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.080
Let's do this again
tomorrow night, Mama.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.300
"Sana-chan sings"

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.300
You brought your
Norinori machine, huh?

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:53.380
♪ We're raking it in
just by being alive. ♪

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.430
♪ Even with nothing else,
we still have our lives. ♪

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.600
♪ Having life proves
that we're alive. ♪

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.600
♪ As long as we're alive,
let's have fun. ♪

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.680
♪ Serious fun, right, and pure. ♪

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.680
♪ Starting today,
our tomorrows are bright. ♪

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.350
♪ The rain will stop,
and the days will be bright. ♪

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.350
Hold it down,
you ignorant jerks!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.360
If you can't be quiet,
I'll knock you flat!

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.030
Think a little about how you're
disturbing the neighbors!

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.030
My name is Kurata,
and we just moved in here today.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.700
Uh, and you are?

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.030
I- I'm Kuma, and I live
in the next room over.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.870
Mister, come join us
in our excitement!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:25.040
You dumb jackass! We're all
miserable because of the rain!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.710
Keep it down in here!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.710
Which is why you should
get stirred up.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.050
Sana, let's get
enthused quietly.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.880
♪ As long as we're alive,
let's have fun. ♪

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.380
♪ Serious fun, with low voices. ♪

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.380
That's just depressing.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.720
Time passes...

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.930
"New Year's Eve comes once a year"

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.060
On New Year's Eve, we eat
soba noodles, soba noodles!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.060
So, this is the end
of this year.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:54.070
I never would have thought we'd be spending
New Year's Eve in a place like this.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.740
The images are starting
to come forward!

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:58.070
I can write! I can write!
I can write like mad!

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.080
You're not using this adversity
as material to write again, are you?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.080
'ulp...

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.910
That's it! I'll write
an essay about all this.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.500
"It was a solemn New Year's Eve."

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.750
"I had never heard
the temple bells sound so sad."

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.090
Oh, that's good,
that's good.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.750
--"Suddenly, an expressionless man came by,
--These folks sure are tough, huh?

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:16.590
--and yelled 'You are being
evicted immediately!'"
--These folks sure are tough, huh?

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:20.260
--I'm going to bed.
--Hey, there's one more page.
Tonight, I'm going to write 108 pages!

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:26.350
"Happy New Year -Babbit"

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:26.770
Happy New Year! This is a New Year's
card from Babbit to all of you!

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.770
Just like that,
the days went by,

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.310
"New school term"

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:30.480
and the new school term started.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.360
Hey, everyone, did you hear about
what happened to Sana-chan's house?

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.650
Mm-hmm. It came out
in the weeklies.

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:38.700
It says that Sana-chan's
whole house got seized.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.450
They're bankrupt, and their
whereabouts are unknown.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.780
"The rumors were spreading"

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:41.950
Rumors spread quickly, huh?

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.030
Good morning!

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:44.700
Sana-chan!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.040
Ah, you're alive!

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.370
Are you okay?

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.040
Say, are you depressed?

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:52.040
Huh? About what?
I'm doing fine!

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.050
But Sana-chan,
your family went b-... b-...

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.710
Boy, these hassaku oranges
are delicious, huh?

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:59.630
Mm-hmm, delicious!
Shall we all share one?

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.050
Oh, you all know about it already?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:06.060
That's right, my family
has gone a bit bankrupt.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:11.060
I- is that true, Sana-chan?
Why did that happen? Aah, poor Sana-chan!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.060
Huh? Am I the only one
who didn't know?

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.070
Yep.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.400
Akito-kun,
Akito-kun,

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.400
did you know, did you know?
Sana-chan's family went bankrupt.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.410
I heard.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.570
You knew?

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:25.910
Yo...

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:26.790
Yo.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.420
You seem... up, huh?

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.580
Yeah...

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.380
"They remembered the kiss..."

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.760
There's a lot to take in.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.260
Listen, you can use these, Sana-chan.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.090
Oh, thanks!
Grateful, grateful!

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.760
We're all in it together
when someone's in trouble, right?

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.430
I'm so happy.
This is a big help.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.430
Here, you can have this.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.770
Even you,
Gomi-kun?

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.270
An eraser,
shaped like a turd?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.110
You've got bad taste,
but I'm still glad for this.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.440
Thank you,
Gomi-kun.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.940
Y- yeah.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.110
Listen, is there
anything else you want?

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:02.240
Hmm, nothing right now.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.740
Say, we should give her
something too, shouldn't we?

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:08.410
Sana-chan's family had everything
taken away from them.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.080
It looks like she doesn't
have anything.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.080
--What would we give her?
--Well, let's see...

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.750
Futons, or blankets, senbei crackers,
chocolate, margarine, nail clippers,

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.420
pocket tissues, animal picture
books, green turtles...

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:25.430
Yes, I'm just confirming
our schedule...

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.930
Huh? Those plans
have fallen through?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.220
I see...

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.270
That's the third one now.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.110
Yum! Yum!

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.610
Sana-chan!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.780
I hoid you were having problems,
that you were in trouble.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.450
It's not all that serious.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:47.780
Let me take care of it. These are costumes,
but you can take them awl if you want.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.120
Uh, thank you. It will help
to have something to wear.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.120
What about food? If you don't eat right,
you won't stay healthy.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:57.130
Oh, they give us these bento
lunches to eat at work.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.800
Oh, but Mama is there
alone in our room.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.130
I knew it.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:03.380
Hey, Uchiyamada!

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:04.720
Toin it ovuh!
Toin it ovuh!

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.720
What?

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.050
That bento.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.720
Sure.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.640
What are you, dumb?

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.730
When I say toin the bento ovuh,
I mean toin it ovuh to Sana-chan!

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:16.730
Oh, that's okay, that's okay. I couldn't
take Uchiyamada-kun's bento away from him.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.730
Uh-uh, that's okay.
I've already eaten six of them.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:21.400
That's why you're so fat!

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.530
"You good boys and girls
eat balanced meals, okay?"

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.650
Do some exercise.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.400
We got a lot of stuff, huh?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.410
But, it's tough,
not having a car.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.370
But this is the weight of everyone's
regard for us. I'm glad.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.410
Sana-chan!

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:39.460
"Sana-chan's drawing song"

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.920
I know this is sudden,
but here's a Sana-chan drawing song.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.500
Get your paper and crayon ready!

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.590
♪ First there comes
a mountain, and then, ♪

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.760
♪ water comes splashing down from it. ♪

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.760
♪ Get two cups ready, ♪

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.760
♪ and then add two handles. ♪

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.760
♪ Butterflies come flying in, ♪

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.760
♪ with tails growing
out of their behinds. ♪

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.100
♪ Here a slope,
there a slope, ups-a-daisy, ♪

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.100
♪ and draw in the eye like an arrow. ♪

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.100
♪ Let's draw one more arrow. ♪

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.110
♪ It's time for gym,
so bring out the vaulting boxes. ♪

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.070
♪ Stick a second one on top of it, ♪

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.070
♪ The letter "ku," the letter "ku,"
the letter "ku," hey! ♪

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:06.360
♪ Then we stick six beans on. ♪

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.410
♪ And now we've drawn Sana-chan! ♪

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.410
♪ Dance! Dance!
Hey! Hey! Hey! ♪

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.870
♪ This is the Sana-chan drawing song! ♪

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.250
Let's see...
perhaps a paid vacation.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.880
"Babbit's drawing song"

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.920
♪ Rice cake, bump, bump,
line, line, triangle, ♪

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.710
♪ raindrop with a heart in it,
draw the wings, ♪

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.090
♪ and it's Babbit! ♪

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:31.930
I came because I was wondering
if you were having any problems.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.220
Well, everyone is being
so nice to me.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.600
Still, there must be a lot
of inconveniences, right?

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.600
If there's anything I can do
for you, feel free to ask.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.770
Thanks.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.240
Huh? Do we have a visitor?

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:50.280
Please leave!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.280
See, the company president
told me to come check on you,

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.620
to make sure you weren't having
any problems, so that's why I'm here.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:01.080
Please leave!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.590
I am grateful for your concern.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:07.880
However, there are many other people
in the world who are living

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:12.390
with far more urgent needs than we have.
We are not all that badly off.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:14.140
Indeed.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:18.230
However, in your present circumstances,
you must have some expenses, right?

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:21.520
"Please accept this money - Yumezono Matata,
President, Dreaming Pro"

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:21.520
This is just a small
token from him.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.900
I said no thank you,
and I meant no thank you!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.610
I will never, for any reason,
accept his money!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.900
Very well.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:33.740
I will leave, for now.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.580
Hey, Sana-chan,
Sagami-san.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.250
We will meet again.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.540
It seems like I've seen that man
with absolutely no taste in clothes

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.420
somewhere before...

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.720
"Who is that?"

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:49.840
Look forward to the answer next time.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:51.590
Well, I don't know
what to say.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:55.600
I came to see if there wasn't
anything I could do for you.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.600
Your concern is more
than enough, Naozumi-kun.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:02.850
But we've already brought home
all of these handouts.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.190
We will just thank you
for the sentiment.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:08.860
Very well. In that case,
please accept my sentiments.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.870
Shut up! You're going
to wake up Ayana-chan!

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.370
S- sorry...

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:18.200
"It's an apartment, after all!"

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.870
But what are we
going to do with this?

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:23.210
We can't very well return it,
and we can't very well throw it out.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.210
There's no harm
in us keeping it.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.840
Seeing as how
you're eating it.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.050
"And so, another morning arrives"

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:30.550
Good morning, Sana.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.550
Good morning, Mama.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.220
Oh, I slept so well.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.550
She's wearing it.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.890
Sana-chan,
you cooked breakfast.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.560
Mm-hmm, we can't afford
to get by in life by relying on others.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.230
Sweet-and-sour pork
flavored with ketchup,

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.060
mixed with bamboo shoots,
rice porridge, and leftover bento.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.730
Such ground-breaking good taste,
your eyeballs might pop out!

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.320
"Now to eat it"

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.440
You're going to eat that?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.570
Mm, this is good,
this is good.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.910
Our eyeballs really might
come popping out,

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.570
it's so bad.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.910
They did eat it!

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.240
Hayama!

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.580
Yo.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.200
It's cold this morning, huh?

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:06.210
Wow, that's an out-of-character
thing for you to say!

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.540
Hey...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.880
It'd be nice...
if it warms up...

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.090
soon...

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.300
It sure would.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.390
Huh?

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.230
Hayama, it's snowing again.

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:32.570
Good morning,
Sana-chan, Akito-kun!

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.400
Ah! I forgot!
I left it inside there!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:39.580
They wouldn't have seized that, too!
I'm going to go get it!

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.910
Sana-chan wouldn't be going
to her old house, would she?

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.750
If she's going to get
something that was seized,

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.080
that will make her a burglar.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:55.260
That commercial
has been cancelled, too?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.930
Yes, I understand.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.850
What's going on here, exactly?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.430
"The Kuratas' former house"

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.980
Sure enough.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.610
We're going, right?
We're going in, right?

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.120
Sana-chan?

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.210
They pasted these slips of paper on?

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:31.210
Mm-hmm. Seems kind of cruel, huh?

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.210
Looks like it happened suddenly.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:37.380
I'll bet they were just having morning tea
when they were chased out.

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:44.890
Sana-chan?

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.770
"Ooh-ooh"

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.570
Sana-chan!

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.230
Oh, I heard a voice, and thought it was
the man from the tax office!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.570
You were hiding?

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.570
"Ooh-ooh" Didn't I look
like a monkey?

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:00.910
Nope.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.820
Be that as it may,
what are you doing here?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.700
What are you doing here?

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.870
Oh, I just forgot
something here.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:08.960
"Forgot something?"

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.040
What?

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:15.210
The power has been shut off,
so it's probably ruined.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:21.340
Thank goodness!
There's still a little left!

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:23.220
Huh?

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:39.190
You came to see that thing?

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:42.570
Well, after all, it does
represent your feelings, Hayama.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:45.240
Your feelings?
What feelings, Akito-kun?

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:46.910
First chop of the year!

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:50.210
But it's too bad you can't
take that with you, huh?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.370
Uh-uh, I just wanted
to see it one more time.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.420
I never even said goodbye.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.760
Hayama...

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.560
Here it comes,
here it comes.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.600
Say, there's still
some film left.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.600
Maybe I should go take pictures
of the things in my room.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.900
Go shoot some memories,
Sana-chan.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:14.900
Is there somebody in here!?

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:15.940
Yikes!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:16.940
Leave this to us.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.610
Who's there!?
Come on out!

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.900
Hey, you!
This place is off-limits!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.910
Hello! I'm the strange young man
who dances everywhere he goes.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:25.950
Akito-kun,
you do it too!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.990
Now, see here! This is no place
for children to be playing!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.630
Thanks for being here with me
up to now, everyone.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.220
Goodbye.

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:50.220
--Hey! You can't play
with the things in this house!
--What do we do now? We run away now.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:54.900
--You're not allowed to ride in that, either!
--What do we do now? We goof around now.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.560
T- that, either...
that, either!

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:02.570
--It's nice to horse around once in a while.
It's nice to horse around once in a while.
--T- that belongs... that belongs to the state!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.240
Tsuyoshi, sounds like she's done.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.700
Huh?
Already?

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.420
Oh, Mister,
you spin real good, huh?

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.590
Those of you who can spin well,
come join Gekidan Komawari!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:21.090
--Did you get them taken?
--Mm-hmm. Thanks.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:24.590
This week's Mama.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.260
This thing is warm!

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:31.770
Thank goodness.

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:33.930
Hayama and Tsuyoshi-kun,
if you hadn't come along,

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:36.100
I might not have been able
to say goodbye to everything.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:38.770
It's not as though
you've lost everything.

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.610
We'll always be together
with you, Sana-chan.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.610
I know that.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:46.280
I may have changed houses,
but as much as before- mm-mm,

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:49.620
even more than before, I feel
like you're here together with me.

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:50.780
That's right.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:55.460
I'm glad this wasn't a dream.
Just by being alive, I'm razoring it in!

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:57.790
That's raking it in,
Sana-chan!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:00.210
What do you mean,
you're canceling again!?

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:01.800
Hello? Hello?

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:10.890
This can't be possible...

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:14.890
Sana-chan doesn't have any work?

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:19.900
Okay, now to work like crazy, take on
a whole bunch of good jobs, and razor it in!

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:23.070
Sana-chan sure is strong, huh?

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:28.910
What about school?

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:38.210
It's all DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:41.040
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:43.130
Bye Bye Bye

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:45.800
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:47.760
and your body will be healthy,

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:49.630
so resolve when to give up

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:51.600
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:52.930
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken)

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:54.600
(Tidak apa-apa,
Nday kambay kambay)

00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:57.230
It's always the same old nonsense,

00:22:57.350 --> 00:22:59.690
U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:02.230
(Mm? Could be you're fairly dumb...)

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:04.900
and then later comes the whimpering,

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:06.780
KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:10.200
(Ah... it's fine, it's fine, it's fine)

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.490
It's all crazy over there,

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:14.410
it's all "waah!" over here,

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:17.750
and the whole Earth
is spinning the wrong way.

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:21.580
So at this point now, yeah at this point now,

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:25.880
you can laugh it away, excuse me, I must be going.

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:27.800
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:30.630
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:32.550
Bye Bye Bye

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:35.430
Cuz you tried your MECHA-KUCHA best,

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.310
to PECHA-KUCHA out a "Hi,"

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:39.270
so just keep going unlike this!

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.140
Wai Wai Wai Wai

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:43.060
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:47.980
Once your lips touch, you can't change your mind.

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:50.650
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.570
and your body will be healthy,

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:54.490
so resolve when to give up

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:58.080
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:00.290
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken,
Tidak apa-apa)

00:24:00.370 --> 00:24:02.290
(Gwaenchansseumnida,
kwenchanayo)

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:03.670
(Mou man tail)

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:10.550
Hoy! In Sana-chan's
next adventures...

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:14.390
That's right, just by being alive,
I'm razoring it in! I mean, raking it in!

00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:18.220
It's okay, it's okay, I'll just "ba-bing"
do a bunch of work! Or so I thought,

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:22.230
but then Sana-chan doesn't have any work.
It's all gone. Even "Child's Toy" is gone.

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:24.060
I can't do anything like this.

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:27.400
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha, Episode 41,
the "is this farewell to a discouraged,

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:29.570
'we're-out-of-everything'
Rei-kun?" installment,

00:24:29.570 --> 00:24:33.570
He Got Me Blacklisted

00:24:33.570 --> 00:24:36.570
Use those New Year's
gifts wisely, now!
